 "note": "Indonesia's largest banks are BRI, Mandiri, BCA and BNI. Mandiri's product summary (RIPLAY, versi umum, read 2026-10-30) gives its common terms (1.75% a month on purchases and cash, a cash advance 6% or 150,000 rupiah, a late payment 1% of the bill at most 100,000, the minimum 5% or 50,000, over the limit 150,000) but leaves each card's membership fee to the card chosen, without a figure, so no Mandiri card is written; BRI's and BNI's card summaries weren't reached in this pass. BCA's product summary for its credit cards (RIPLAY, in force from 19 August 2026, read again 2026-10-30): purchases and cash 1.75% a month; each card's main-card annual fee: 125,000 rupiah for the Everyday, UnionPay, tiket.com, Blibli, Visa Batman and Mastercard Globe cards, 250,000 for BCA Card Platinum, 450,000 for the JCB, Visa and Mastercard Black, 500,000 for the KrisFlyer Visa Signature, 1,000,000 for the KrisFlyer Visa Infinite and Mastercard World, 2,000,000 for the PPS Club Visa Infinite, and none for BCA Kartu Kredit Indonesia (the QR-only card issued alongside a BCA Card, with no cash advance); a cash advance 3% (Everyday and Platinum) or 4% of the amount, at least 40,000 rupiah, the summary's range read that way; over the limit up to 40,000 rupiah, nothing on the Platinum to KKI cards, written as 40,000 on the six others; a late payment 1% of the total bill, at most 100,000 (written as a share of the balance); the minimum payment 5% of the bill. The 20,000-rupiah counter fee on a cash advance, stamp duty, card replacement and statement fees aren't written. The summary states no foreign-transaction fee or grace period. Wave 4 (2026-10-30): CIMB Niaga, one of the largest card issuers, and Bank Mega, a large card issuer (the Transmart and Metro co-brands), are added, both publishing each card's fees; BRI's, BNI's and BTN's sites answer Incapsula's block, OCBC Indonesia's carries Incapsula, and Permata's answers 403 (2026-10-30). CIMB Niaga's conventional credit card tariffs and fees page (read 2026-10-30): the main card's annual fee, JCB Ultimate, Mastercard World and World ALL Accor 3,000,000 rupiah, World Cathay and Visa Infinite 1,500,000, JCB Precious, Visa Travel Card and Platinum ALL Accor 350,000, Visa Gold 250,000, Visa Classic 125,000; the Preferred Visa Infinite, Mastercard Platinum, JCB Platinum, Mastercard Gold, Mastercard Classic and both OCTO Cards none (the Mastercard World's waiver for Preferred customers with 500 million rupiah isn't written; the CIMB Private Wealth card, for Private Wealth customers only, isn't written); the OCTO Card with a physical card 10,000 rupiah a month; the Kartu Kredit Indonesia free its first year, then free with 3 million rupiah spent or 150,000 rupiah (written as a yearly fee waived the first year or by that spending); purchases and cash 1.75% a month (21% a year); the minimum payment 5%, at least 100,000 rupiah on the seven top cards and 50,000 on the rest, extended by Bank Indonesia's policy to 31 December 2026; a late payment 1% of the total bill, at least 75,000 and at most 100,000; a cash withdrawal 6%, at least 300,000 (top cards) or 150,000, with none on the OCTO Card Digital and KKI; over the limit 250,000 (to the Platinum ALL Accor) or 200,000. Payment-channel, statement, notification and stamp fees aren't written; no foreign-transaction fee or grace period is stated. Bank Mega's product summary for its credit cards (RIPLAY - Kartu Kredit, read 2026-10-30): the main card's annual fee, Mega Travel Card 1 million rupiah, Visa Platinum 750,000, Visa Gold 450,000, Visa Classic 400,000, Metro 500,000, Transmart Platinum 500,000, Transmart Classic 450,000, each free its first year as each card's own section states; the BLIV Card 30,000 a month; purchases and cash 1.75% a month (21% a year); a cash withdrawal 6%, at least 200,000 (Travel), 175,000 (Platinum, Metro and both Transmart cards) or 125,000 (Gold, Classic, BLIV); a late payment 1% of the bill, at most 100,000; over the limit 250,000. The MegaFirst Infinite, free while the holder is a MegaFirst customer, and the corporate card aren't written. The summary states no minimum payment or foreign-transaction fee; the due date 25 days after the statement isn't a grace period and isn't written.",
